    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "From the project, I have learned that both PCA and t-SNE are useful tools when it comes to reduction. PCA is a lot faster than t-SNE and is more light weight which makes it good especially when dealing with huge datasets because of its compression quality. T-SNE is more useful when we want to see clear separation between different cluster groups. It is the better option when it comes to visualization, though it runs a lot slower, hence we had to run a subset of it in the project. Reduction is useful when it comes to making models with a large number of dimensions because it makes it easier to make predictions because values are in a smaller space, which reduces overfitting."
